{"tool_name":"biscuit","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"biscuit","version":"1.10.2.20260818","home":"https://github.com/huishenlab/biscuit","documentation":"https://huishenlab.github.io/biscuit","license":"MIT","summary":"A utility for analyzing sodium bisulfite conversion-based DNA methylation/modification data.","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/nar/gkae097","biotools:biscuit"],"license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"number":0,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":["make","cmake",null,null],"host":["zlib","ncurses","pthread-stubs","libcurl","libdeflate"],"run":["pthread-stubs","perl"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/huishenlab/biscuit/releases/download/v1.10.2.20260818/release-source.zip","test":{"commands":["biscuit 2>&1 | grep \"Usage\"","QC.sh -h 2>&1 | grep \"Usage\"","build_biscuit_QC_assets.pl -h 2>&1 | grep \"Usage\""]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"biscuit","identifiers":["doi:10.5281/zenodo.48262"],"license":"MIT","summary":"A utility for analyzing sodium bisulfite conversion-based DNA methylation/modification data","home_url":"https://github.com/huishenlab/biscuit","keywords":[],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":46},"biotools":{"id":"biscuit","home":"https://huishenlab.github.io/biscuit/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"An efficient, standards-compliant tool suite for simultaneous genetic and epigenetic inference in bulk and single-cell studies.","addition_date":"2024-05-24T10:48:53.697269Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T13:55:47.504931Z","tool_type":["Suite"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:biscuit","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"hui.shen@vai.org","name":"Hui Shen","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9767-4084","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"jacob.morrison@vai.org","name":"Jacob Morrison","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8592-4744","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Bisulfite mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3186"},{"term":"Genome indexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3211"},{"term":"Imputation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3557"},{"term":"Methylation calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3919"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"BISCUIT","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkae097","metadata":{"abstract":"Data from both bulk and single-cell whole-genome DNA methylation experiments are under-utilized in many ways. This is attributable to inefficient mapping of methylation sequencing reads, routinely discarded genetic information, and neglected read-level epigenetic and genetic linkage information. We introduce the BISulfite-seq Command line User Interface Toolkit (BISCUIT) and its companion R/Bioconductor package, biscuiteer, for simultaneous extraction of genetic and epigenetic information from bulk and single-cell DNA methylation sequencing. BISCUIT's performance, flexibility and standards-compliant output allow large, complex experimental designs to be characterized on clinical timescales. BISCUIT is particularly suited for processing data from single-cell DNA methylation assays, with its excellent scalability, efficiency, and ability to greatly enhance mappability, a key challenge for single-cell studies. We also introduce the epiBED format for single-molecule analysis of coupled epigenetic and genetic information, facilitating the study of cellular and tissue heterogeneity from DNA methylation sequencing.","authors":[{"name":"Beddows I."},{"name":"Berman B.P."},{"name":"Eapen J."},{"name":"Habib W.A."},{"name":"Heo L."},{"name":"Johnson B.K."},{"name":"Katsman E."},{"name":"Laird P.W."},{"name":"Morrison J."},{"name":"Semwal A."},{"name":"Shen H."},{"name":"Triche T.J."},{"name":"Zhou W."}],"citationCount":3,"date":"2024-04-12T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"BISCUIT: An e